 "notes": [
  "Source: StockAnalysis.com, pages fetched 2026-11-13. Values are as displayed on each page, in the page's currency and unit (see per-company currency/unit); no currency conversion, nothing computed.",
  "Income items (revenue, gross_profit, operating_income, net_income, rd) are read from the HTML table of the /financials/income-statement/ page (the bare /financials/ URL is now an overview page without R&D).",
  "operating_cash_flow is read from the HTML table of the cash-flow page. capex and fcf rows are not in the server-rendered HTML table (it stops at Operating Cash Flow); they are taken from the data payload embedded in the same page (rows 'Capital Expenditures' and 'Free Cash Flow'), which is in raw currency units and was divided by 1,000,000 to match the page's displayed unit.",
  "capex is stored positive; the page shows it as a negative number (cash outflow).",
  "ttm.cashflow_period_end is the period end of the cash-flow column used. fy2022 is the column the page labels 'FY 2022'; for companies with offset fiscal years this may end in early 2022 (see company notes).",
  "ttm.period_basis is 'TTM' or, where the page has no separate TTM column because the latest quarter is the fiscal year-end (micron, apple, intuit, accenture), the latest fiscal year label.",
  "Null fields: rd is null for skhynix, vertiv, tencent, accenture (no Research & Development line on page); capex is null for applovin. All 84 pages loaded (HTTP 200)."
 ]
